Subject: [PATCH 3/3] 071 (3/3): SALVO listed at stu32-arcade 5947c16, the
 sixth game; its board script

Michael's ruling on the games plan (abacus #8569): a fixed-screen space shooter, Galaga-style,
in space. The ship moves with 4 or SOFT1 and 6 or SOFT6 and fires with 8, ENTER, 9, x or +,
held; 32 aliens come in, sway and dive; three ships, an extra one every 10,000 points.
Its manifest says GAMES; until the folder menu (unit 072) it sits in APPS like the rest, on
the second page after MINES. device/standin/salvo.txt starts a game, holds 6 and 8 together,
and leaves the ship to be lost. work/071-games.md has the unit's checks and numbers (all
three commits): +6,128 B flash on the stand-in, +6,160 on Rev A, +0 internal RAM.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
